    "rulings": [
      "Ruling: select general finite nonzero preparation instead of unit-only author admission \u2014 framework absorbs numerical work and accepts ordinary vectors. Cost if wrong: tagged reference/native qualification must reject unsupported representations rather than weaken readback.",
      "Ruling: preserve constructor refusal and add explicit version-bound constructor \u2014 avoids changing existing generation semantics. Cost if wrong: applications must explicitly select the new profile.",
      "Ruling: reject zero Cosine before dispatch \u2014 mathematical direction undefined; avoids claiming Qdrant's zero score is mathematical Cosine. Cost if wrong: hosts must handle zero embeddings explicitly.",
      "Ruling: qualification is the pinned native image/default floating-point environment; safe references model eligible CPU paths without claiming arbitrary server builds or ARM execution. Cost if wrong: unknown build/environment cannot use native acceptance evidence.",
      "Ruling: signed-zero preservation applies to approved input and provider-preparation output \u2014 core author admission already canonicalizes input zero, which must remain stable. Cost if wrong: claiming preservation of raw author -0 would contradict existing core contract.",
      "Ruling: preserve inactive old temporary-package rlib/rmeta caches with byte-identical archives before retiring working copies \u2014 needed to retain native disk protection; source/native data/final executables untouched. Cost if wrong: a still-needed compiler library is regenerated by the verifier, while its previous bytes remain archived.",
      "Ruling: perform review before full freeze and retain two Minor findings \u2014 no current source defect identified; full verifier remains publication gate. Cost if wrong: later source fixes require fresh affected/full verification; weaker future regression protection and ambiguous enum prose remain documented."
    ],
